\\\ -5x+3y+7z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $y=-1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-19,$ find the value of $k.$" 13194139535374 true] [17592186346467 1113 #uuid "cb48b856-28da-5ef9-a5c0-dcc3cc94f523" 13194139535374 true] [17592186346467 1145 "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -3 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}|+(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(7k-6)-(14-15)-5(-4+5k) \\\\  & =21k-18+1+20-25k \\\\  & =-4k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{-4k+3}{-19}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=-1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4k+3}{-19} & =-1 \\\\ -4k+3 & =19 \\\\ -4k & =16 \\\\ k & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346469 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346470 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346471 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346472 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346473 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1041 "selection" 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346473 13194139535374 true] [17592186346468 1110 #uuid "b90e78f8-d525-5131-8c50-118e29fcbf1c" 13194139535374 true] [17592186346469 1034 "k=2" 13194139535374 true] [17592186346469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535374 true] [17592186346469 1111 #uuid "89297b27-f64d-5d33-